wg-shield-recovery-ftl-locked = FTL lockout · Waiting for jump cooldown to finish.
wg-shield-gun-lock = GUNS LOCKED · { $seconds } s
wg-shield-gun-lock-help = Heat overran the shield generator and the field collapsed; the ship's guns stay locked until the countdown ends. Lowering shields or venting yourself never locks them.
wg-shield-gun-lock-popup = Shield field collapsed! Ship guns locked for { $seconds } seconds.
wg-shield-gun-hold = GUNS HOLDING · TOO HOT
wg-shield-gun-hold-help = The ship is too hot to fire. Every shot heats the ship, shields or none. Guns fire again once it cools; venting cools it fastest.
wg-shield-helm-vent = Vent heat
wg-shield-helm-vent-help = Dumps the ship's heat fast. Shields drop and guns can't fire until no heat is left, and it can't be called off. Every radar in range shows the ship venting. An overloaded shield generator can't vent until its overload ends.
wg-shield-helm-hard-heat-help = The ship's heat. The bright part is hard heat: damage the field absorbed. Under a raised field it stays until { $hold } seconds have passed without a hit; lower the field or vent to lose it sooner. The rest is soft heat: every shot your guns fire adds some, shields or none, and it cools by itself. Past the red line the guns hold fire until the ship cools. The hotter the ship, the farther off long-range sensors pick it up.
wg-shield-venting = VENTING · GUNS OFFLINE · { $seconds } s
wg-shield-venting-untimed = VENTING · GUNS OFFLINE
wg-shield-venting-help = The ship is venting heat. Shields stay down and guns can't fire until no heat is left.
wg-shield-vent-popup = Venting heat! Shields down, guns offline.
